Here's a design for a 1B dense-equivalent MoE (8 experts, top-2 ⇒ ~1B active / ~2.1B total params, matching dense-1B FLOPs with a ~2× parameter overhead, Mixtral-style routing).

```json
{
  "framework": "DeepSpeed-MoE (Megatron-LM backend, ZeRO-2 + expert parallelism)",
  "architecture": {
    "hidden_size": 2048,
    "num_layers": 24,
    "num_attention_heads": 16,
    "head_dim": 128,
    "intermediate_size": 2048,
    "num_experts": 8,
    "top_k": 2,
    "capacity_factor": 1.25,
    "dropout": 0.0,
    "position_embedding": "rope",
    "router": "softmax top-k, load-balancing auxiliary loss (0.001)",
    "vocab_size": 50272,
    "seq_len": 4096,
    "active_params_est": "~0.9B",
    "total_params_est": "~2.1B"
  },
  "parallelism": {
    "world_size": 8,
    "data_parallel": 2,
    "expert_parallel": 4,
    "tensor_parallel": 1,
    "pipeline_parallel": 1,
    "gate_recompute": true,
    "drop_tokens": false
  },
  "batch_size": {
    "micro_batch": 2,
    "per_gpu": 2,
    "global": 32,
    "effective_batch_tokens": 131072
  },
  "training": {
    "optimizer": "AdamW (fp32 states, ZeRO-2)",
    "lr": 3e-4,
    "lr_schedule": "cosine with 2000-step warmup",
    "weight_decay": 0.1,
    "bf16": true,
    "grad_clip": 1.0,
    "seq_len": 4096
  },
  "estimated_memory_gb": 24,
  "estimated_tokens_per_sec": 45000,
  "launch_notes": "Run with `deepspeed --num_gpus=8 train.py --deepspeed_config ds_moe.json`. EP=4 with 8 experts places 2 experts per GPU (1 replica across ranks), DP=2 for optimizer-state sharding and load balancing. Configure `deepspeed_moe_top_k=2`, `capacity_factor=1.25` (25% slack absorbs router imbalance; if dropout tokens >1% raise to 1.5). Use `disable_moe_aux_loss`=false so the load-balancing loss prevents expert collapse. bf16 + ZeRO-2 keeps memory ~24 GB/GPU on 8×A100 80GB; raise capacity factor or reduce micro_batch if memory-bound. Estimated throughput 45k tok/s assumes A100-80GB, ~35k tok/s on H100 if EP-bound router sync dominates."
}
```

Key tradeoffs: top-2/8 with capacity 1.25 gives ~2× total parameters for ~1× dense-1B compute — the standard cost/quality sweet spot. EP=4 (2 experts/rank) with DP=2 keeps router all-to-all cheap while sharding the ~17 GB of Adam states.